{{ElectionsWY}}
The '''1996 United States Senate election in Wyoming''' was held November 5, 1996. Incumbent Republican U.S. Senator [[Alan K. Simpson]] decided to retire. Republican nominee [[Mike Enzi]] won the open seat. This is the last time a Democrat won 40% of the vote in an election for either of Wyoming's US Senate seats. Indeed, only one subsequent Democratic nominee was able to earn 30% of the vote, [[Gary Trauner]] in [[2018 United States Senate election in Wyoming|2018]].

